name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q13_2025'

question 'When building a search function, why should you "refine" AI-generated test cases?'

right 'AI-generated tests always focus on the easiest possible scenarios and might miss complex "edge cases" or "inclusivity" gaps.'
wrong 'AI-generated tests are usually written in a different version of JavaScript.'
wrong ' You should never refine them; the AI knows better than the human developer.'
wrong 'Refining them is the only way to make the tests run faster.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 9

AI often generates "happy path" tests (standard inputs). Humans must refine those tests to cover edge cases and ensure the search logic doesn't unfairly exclude certain terms or groups.
MARKDOWN
